  <row>
    <panel>
      <html>
        <h1>dCloud Splunk Lab</h1>
        <p>
          A self-rebuilding Splunk lab for Cisco dCloud. The environment resets to an
          empty template each session, so on every startup a script pulls this project
          from GitHub and re-creates the full configuration from scratch. Nothing here is
          configured by hand - it is all code, so the lab is identical every time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Location-based access control (RBAC) is the <b>foundation</b> the lab is built on -
          each location's data lives in its own indexes and roles grant access per location -
          but the lab is a general demo platform, not only about RBAC.
        </p>
        <p>
          <b>Repository:</b>
          <a href="https://github.com/js-csco/splunk-dcloud" target="_blank">github.com/js-csco/splunk-dcloud</a>
        </p>
        <h3>What gets pre-loaded on each session</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><b>6 indexes</b>, one namespace per location: london_* (London), berlin_* (Berlin), loc1_* (infra)</li>
          <li><b>3 roles</b>: role_london (London only), role_berlin (Berlin only), role_global (everything)</li>
          <li><b>3 users</b>: Leo (London), Ben (Berlin), Gary (global)</li>
          <li><b>Dashboards</b>: Lab Info (this page), Setup Status, Ingestion &amp; Health</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Start here, then open <b>Setup Status</b> to confirm everything loaded correctly
          before the demo begins.
        </p>
      </html>
    </panel>
  </row>

